  ('palisades-tahoe-california', '12A', 'Palisades Tahoe (Olympic Valley)', 'United States', 'The 1960 Olympic mountain, now two peaks on one', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Pacific Coast', '{"ski","romance","family","culinary","wellness","entertainment","adventure"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Palisades Tahoe = Alterra / Ikon; RENAMED from ''Squaw Valley'' in 2021 (the resort concluded the term is a racist/sexist slur; Washoe Tribe sought removal; ''Palisades'' = the granite cliffs) - use the old name ONLY as history","HOSTED THE 1960 WINTER OLYMPICS (founder Alexander Cushing; California Historical Landmark No. 724); Olympic Valley identity endures","ONE COMBINED ~6,000-acre resort (''8 Peaks, 1 Story''): Palisades (Olympic Valley) + Alpine Meadows joined by the Base-to-Base Gondola (opened 2022); 288 trails, 39 lifts, base 6,200 / summit 9,050 / 2,850 ft vertical; ~400 in snow; no night skiing","110-person Aerial Tram to High Camp (8,200 ft; year-round sightseeing/dining/seasonal pool+skating); the ONLY North American resort with a gondola, a funitel AND an aerial tram","Famous STEEP, cliff-lined expert terrain + extreme-skiing pedigree (Palisades side); mellower tree-lined Alpine Meadows side - two characters on one pass","US-TRAFFIC CANDOR: ~600,000 skier-visits/yr is a Wikipedia/consensus ESTIMATE, not audited - consensus only","RNO ~42 mi (~45-60 min); Sacramento ~96 mi; SF ~196 mi via I-80/Donner; free TART buses + North Lake Tahoe Express shuttle + JSX","NO on-site cat/heli (steep in-bounds + regional guided touring); NO natural hot springs (Grover Hot Springs ~70+ mi / 1.5-2 hr day-trip; High Camp/Village tubs man-made); Ritz-Carlton Lake Tahoe is at Northstar (separate); Ikon/lift prices dynamic"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police/fire/medical/rescue dispatch); alert ski patrol on-mountain","hospital":"Tahoe Forest Hospital, Truckee - critical-access hospital, 24-hr ER (~10-15 m