  ('stowe-vermont', '12A', 'Stowe', 'United States', 'Vermont''s highest peak, the East''s toughest four runs, and', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'New England', '{"ski","romance","culinary","family","adventure","entertainment","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Stowe = Vail Resorts / Epic (acquired Feb 2017); on MOUNT MANSFIELD (Vermont''s highest peak, 4,395 ft) + Spruce Peak, linked by the Over Easy gondola; lift-served summit ~3,700 ft, base ~1,559 ft, ~2,360 ft vertical","485 acres, 116 trails, ~12 lifts (2 gondolas); the legendary ''FRONT FOUR'' (Goat, Starr, National, Liftline) - among the toughest lift-served runs in the East; longest run Toll Road 4.3 mi; ~224 in snow + 83% snowmaking; no night skiing; 4 terrain parks","RESORT vs TOWN: the classic town of Stowe (''the Ski Capital of the East'') is ~7 mi away via the VT-108 Mountain Road - it holds the village (church steeple, covered bridges), inns + the Trapp Family Lodge","Lodge at Spruce Peak = marquee slope-side luxury (self-described ''4-diamond'', full spa); Trapp Family Lodge (Sound-of-Music von Trapps) = Austrian-style 2,600-ac estate IN THE TOWN (not the resort) with premier Nordic (167 km) + von Trapp Brewing","US-TRAFFIC CANDOR: marquee Eastern resort but Vail reports visitation only in aggregate - no per-resort count published - consensus only","BTV ~45 min / ~35 mi (verify); Boston ~3.5 hr, Montreal ~2-2.5 hr, NYC ~5-6 hr drive; a marquee FALL-FOLIAGE town (second major season, late Sep-mid Oct)","NO on-site cat/heli (fully lift-served; Mansfield backcountry - Bruce/Teardrop trails - is self-guided/separate); NO natural hot springs (none on Mansfield/at Stowe); NO avalanche center (low-avalanche Eastern terrain - Mt Washington Avalanche Center is a different NH mountain)","Altitude LOW (no AMS factor); winter spine = Eastern ice/hardpack + extreme cold/wind chill on Mansfield + VT-108 Mountain Road winter driving (